@model CommunityHub.Pages.McSubscribeToggle
@*
    §383 — the per-box subscribe/unsubscribe control (operator 2026-07-26: "a subscribe/unsubscribe
    ratio button next to #2 & #3 which is turned ON by default").

    A SUBMIT BUTTON, not a checkbox: the state changes server-side the moment it is pressed, and a
    checkbox would either need JS to post itself or a separate Save — both of which leave the screen
    disagreeing with the database for a while. The button's label states the state it is IN and the
    action moves to the other one, so there is never any doubt which way round it is.

    §420 (operator 2026-07-27: "nothing happens when i click mail notifications on/off - how can a
    person switch this themselves then and turn off ?"). This partial USED to assume it was
    "rendered inside the page's ONE form" and emitted a bare <button type="submit">. It was not:
    on /MasterClassPage both toggles sit ABOVE the page's only form (the Q&A comment box), and a
    submit button outside a form does nothing at all — no request, no error, no clue.

    It now carries its OWN <form>. That is safe here and does NOT violate §304b, which is about
    NESTED forms: these two are siblings of the comment form, never inside it. Owning the form also
    means the control cannot be broken again by moving it, which is exactly how it broke.
*@
<form method="post" style="margin:0;">
<button type="submit"
        asp-page-handler="Subscription"
        asp-route-sessionId="@Model.SessionId"
        asp-route-t="@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.Token) ? null : Model.Token)"
        asp-route-kind="@Model.Kind"
        asp-route-subscribed="@(!Model.Subscribed)"
        title="@(Model.Subscribed ? "Turn these e-mails off" : "Turn these e-mails on")"
        style="flex:0 0 auto;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;cursor:pointer;
               font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:999px;
               background:@(Model.Subscribed ? "#ecfdf5" : "#f3f4f6");
               color:@(Model.Subscribed ? "#15803d" : "#6b7280");
               border:1px solid @(Model.Subscribed ? "#a7f3d0" : "#d7dee8");">
    <span aria-hidden="true">@(Model.Subscribed ? "🔔" : "🔕")</span>
    @* §412 (operator 2026-07-27: "add the word Mail here in front"). "Notifications" alone reads as
       in-app or push; this toggle only ever controls E-MAIL, and that word is what tells someone
       whether switching it off stops something landing in their inbox. *@
    <span>@(Model.Subscribed ? "Mail notifications on" : "Mail notifications off")</span>
</button>
</form>
<span class="sr-only">@Model.Description</span>
